Modifications vs. reference
---------------------------
1. Import paths: gvisor.dev/gvisor/tools/... rewritten to
   logos/nogo/internal/... throughout. No gvisor.dev imports remain in
   build code. (Three string literals in internal/check/check_test.go and
   analyzer path-matching literals/comments in checklocks and checkimports
   intentionally keep gvisor.dev paths: they are synthetic fixture package
   paths and match-targets ported verbatim from reference tests, not
   imports.)
2. Flag shim: gvisor.dev/gvisor/runsc/flag is a pure alias wrapper over the
   standard flag package (runsc/flag/flag.go); the port uses stdlib flag
   directly. Behavior is identical.
3. Archive shim: gvisor.dev/gvisor/pkg/zip is a pure alias wrapper over
   stdlib archive/zip; the facts bundle port uses archive/zip directly.
4. Bazel-only surfaces dropped: defs.bzl wiring, bundle/filter/render
   subcommands, FindRoots/SplitStdPackages/FilterStdPackages stdlib-bundle
   helpers, and GOVERSIONModFile-driven flows kept as a var only (cmd/go
   passes -GOVERSION directly). The per-package run (reference `check`
   command: -package plus -import/-archive/-facts/-bundle maps and
   GOOS/GOARCH/GOVERSION/tags/race/msan target flags) is preserved in
   cmd/logos-nogo.
5. Registry: internal/check/analyzers.go keeps the exact 25 x/tools vet
   passes, 6 custom analyzers, and all five honnef families
   (quickfix/simple/staticcheck/stylecheck/unused) with the reference gob
   FactType pre-registration and transitive Requires closure, plus a
   deterministic sorted census accessor for `-list`.
6. CLI: cmd/logos-nogo exposes -list (deterministic census), -V=full (go
   vet tool-identity protocol: executable path plus sha256 content hash),
   and the real per-package run emitting the package facts file and the
   findings set (gob default, -json, or -text). Analysis errors exit
   nonzero without outputs; per-analyzer panics stay visible as error
   findings via the driver's recovery path and are never reported clean.

